WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.026
Five houses hold 2, 7, 9, 3 and 1, but neighbours share an alarm.

00:07.026 --> 00:14.700
Trying all 32 sets of houses rechecks the same endings again and again.

00:15.000 --> 00:24.692
Write down the best haul for the first house, then the first two.

00:24.692 --> 00:31.700
Each answer only needs the two cells before it.

00:32.000 --> 00:42.467
At house 2, skipping keeps 7 but taking adds its 9 to 2.

00:42.467 --> 00:47.700
Taking wins, so dp[3] is 11.

00:48.000 --> 00:51.770
One pass fills the row: O(n).

00:51.770 --> 00:57.880
The last cell reads 12, from houses 0, 2 and 4.

00:57.880 --> 00:59.700
That’s 1-D DP.
